{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-439344-r4587203","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Koesisters with Coconut","sourcePageId":439344,"sourceRevision":"4587203","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-10-26T23:28:14Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Codename Noreste","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Koesisters%20with%20Coconut&oldid=4587203","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:07:15.213Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Fried recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for fritters","Category:Recipes for pastries","Category:Recipes using baking powder","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using cake flour","Category:Recipes using cardamom","Category:Recipes using cinnamon","Category:Recipes using coconut","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using ground ginger","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes using milk","Category:Recipes using superfine sugar","Category:Recipes using tangerine","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:South African recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"728b0a80598cdfc249175079ca3fa47fdef1e3d46f035064fd9276dd84a3c628","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Yield = About 40 fritters\n| Difficulty = 3\n| Image = [[File:Koesisters Cape Malay South Africa.jpg|300px]]\n}}{{Recipe}}\n\n'''Koesisters''' are a South African Cape Malay doughnut soaked in syrup and sprinkled with coconut.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n=== Fritters ===\n* 6 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] (700 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) cake [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Superfine Sugar|castor sugar]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n* 3 teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* 2 tablespoon ground [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n* 2 teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Aniseed|aniseed]]\n* 1 teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Cardamom|cardamom]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]] \n* 10 g instant [[Cookbook:Yeast|yeast]] \n* 1 tablespoon dried and ground [[Cookbook:Tangerine|tangerine]] peel (optional; can use [[Cookbook:Orange|orange]] [[Cookbook:Zest|zest]] instead)\n* 250 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] lukewarm [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n* 100 g [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]] or [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]], beaten\n* About 2 cups lukewarm [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n* [[Cookbook:Oil|Oil]] for deep frying\n\n=== Syrup ===\n* 5 pieces cinnamon stick\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]] \n* 2 cups water\n* 1 cup desiccated [[Cookbook:Coconut|coconut]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# [[Cookbook:Sifting|Sift]] the dry ingredients together into a bowl, and make a well in the centre.\n# Warm milk and butter until lukewarm and then add the beaten egg. Pour mixture into dry ingredients along with enough lukewarm water, and mix to form a soft [[Cookbook:Dough|dough]].\n# Cover and leave the dough to rise in warm place until doubled in size.\n# Take small amounts of dough and form into oval-shaped balls.\n# [[Cookbook:Deep Frying|Deep fry]] dough in oil on medium heat (180 °C) until evenly browned. Remove onto [[Cookbook:Paper Towel|paper towels]] to cool (around 30 minutes).\n# Heat the sugar, cinnamon sticks, and water on a low heat, stirring continuously until a thick [[Cookbook:Syrup|syrup]] forms.\n# Once the koesisters are cool, soak in bubbling syrup for 1 minute.\n# Take them out of the syrup and sprinkle with coconut.\n\n[[Category:South African recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes for fritters]]\n[[Category:Fried recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pastries]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coconut]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using superfine sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cardamom]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tangerine]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cake flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]\n[[Category:Recipes using milk]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Koesisters with Coconut","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"6 cups (700 g) cake flour","sourceText":"6 cups (700 g) cake flour","amountText":"6 cups (700 g) cake flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 tablespoon castor sugar","sourceText":"1 tablespoon castor sugar","amountText":"1 tablespoon castor sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 teaspoon baking powder","sourceText":"1 teaspoon baking powder","amountText":"1 teaspoon baking powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"3 teaspoon ground cinnamon","sourceText":"3 teaspoon ground cinnamon","amountText":"3 teaspoon ground cinnamon","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"2 tablespoon ground ginger","sourceText":"2 tablespoon ground ginger","amountText":"2 tablespoon ground ginger","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"2 teaspoon ground aniseed","sourceText":"2 teaspoon ground aniseed","amountText":"2 teaspoo